      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Conclusion**\n",
        "\n",
        "In this project, we developed a logistic regression model to predict the likelihood of individuals being at risk of heart disease using a health behavior dataset. The dataset was carefully explored and preprocessed, including handling missing values, feature selection, and encoding where necessary. Exploratory data analysis (EDA) helped uncover key patterns and relationships between features such as age, BMI, physical activity, and smoking habits with heart disease.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model was trained on a portion of the data and evaluated on the remaining test set. Performance metrics like accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score indicated that the model is capable of effectively identifying individuals at risk. Visualizations such as pairplots and histograms further supported the model's assumptions and clarified data distributions.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, the project demonstrated that logistic regression provides a solid baseline for heart disease prediction due to its simplicity, interpretability, and reasonable accuracy, making it a suitable choice for public health risk assessment and early intervention initiatives."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HZue2UXtH-BI"
      }
